    clientVision: 'An international family of discerning investors acquired this full-floor penthouse atop the Regalia in Sunny Isles Beach as their primary winter residence. They mandated a complete turnkey realization of world-class caliber: an interior that matched the building\'s organic architecture without competing with the jaw-dropping 360-degree ocean and intracoastal vistas. The client required absolute white-glove delivery, asking the studio to oversee every facet down to custom monogrammed linens, Hermès porcelain, and curated international art. Their vision prioritized tactile, organic luxury, sophisticated entertaining zones, and an effortless transition between breezy morning coffee on deep cantilevered terraces and formal black-tie dinners overlooking the illuminated coastline.',
    designChallenge: 'Occupying the 45th floor wrapped entirely in undulating curvilinear glass presents extraordinary spatial, solar, and logistics hurdles. The curvilinear perimeter meant that standard rectilinear furniture felt jarring and misaligned, requiring bespoke curved millwork and custom seating radii tailored to the facade. Solar radiation and maritime glare at this altitude are intense, demanding complex dual-motorized Lutron solar systems concealed within razor-thin architectural ceiling pockets. Furthermore, transporting ten-foot marble slabs, custom oversized sofas, and bespoke Italian millwork up exterior construction hoists and through tight freight elevators required meticulous millimeter planning and close coordination with condominium engineering.',
    approach: 'Paula & Amanda Ambrósio resolved the organic geometry by designing custom curved architectural elements that mirror the tower\'s iconic wave-like terraces. In the grand salon, we composed a bespoke semicircular sectional upholstered in textured sand bouclé, paired with organic-edge cocktail tables sculpted from bookmatched Taj Mahal quartzite and brushed champagne bronze bases.\n\nTo anchor the boundless glass perimeter, we introduced an interior spine of rich Canaletto walnut paneling featuring subtle bronze shadowline reveals. These wood planes conceal elevator access, private suite portals, and high-capacity air conditioning systems while imparting warmth and acoustic grounding to the high-altitude space.\n\nThe culinary zone was designed as both an architectural sculpture and a high-performance chef\'s kitchen. The monolithic island features double waterfall quartzite slabs with mitered seamless edges and an integrated breakfast bar. The adjacent formal dining salon is centered around an undulating bronze branch chandelier whose crystal globes emulate ocean spray, suspended over an eleven-foot hand-waxed dining table.\n\nIn the primary wing, the bedroom was oriented to catch the Atlantic sunrise. We designed a wrap-around headboard wall in hand-stitched leather panels with integrated bronze sconces and motorized drapery pockets. The adjoining spa bath was completely transformed with bookmatched slab walls and a freestanding sculptural tub elevated on a limestone plinth facing the endless horizon.',
    materialsNarrative: 'The material curation reflects the interplay of sand, water, and sky. We selected Italian Canaletto walnut for its chocolate undertones and stable response to ocean humidity, pairing it with honed Taj Mahal quartzite and Roman silver travertine. Fabrics were sourced from Loro Piana Interiors, featuring superfine wools, washed Belgian linens, and raw silk bouclés that resist UV fading. Architectural hardware was custom cast in solid bronze with a hand-rubbed living patina that gracefully weathers coastal air.',
    materialsDetails: [
      'Italian Canaletto Walnut wall cladding with shadowline bronze reveals',
      'Taj Mahal Quartzite waterfall countertops and custom coffee tables',
      'Imported Loro Piana cashmere and Belgian linen custom drapery',
      'Hand-applied microcement ceiling finishes and architectural low-glare downlights',
      'Custom curved Italian modular seating crafted specifically to the building\'s radial geometry'
    ],
    result: 'The Regalia Penthouse stands as one of the most magnificent turnkey achievements along the South Florida coastline. The owners arrived with their luggage to a fully illuminated, perfectly curated residence with fresh florals, chilled wine, and every domestic amenity operational from the very first evening. The interior feels deeply peaceful and anchored, turning the breathtaking 360-degree ocean views into an organic extension of the living spaces. It exemplifies how rigorous turnkey interior architecture can achieve absolute bespoke luxury without burdening the client with logistical stress.',
