    clientVision: 'The clients, a young multi-child family relocating to Williams Island in Aventura, sought a dynamic home that resolved a common residential dilemma: how to create a sophisticated, quiet-luxury environment for adult entertaining while celebrating joyful, imaginative spaces for young children. They wanted the public entertaining salons to feel elevated, serene, and grounded in noble organic materials, yet completely functional for family life without fear of delicate surfaces. For the children\'s wing, they requested imaginative custom themed suites and study areas that inspire creativity and play, constructed with durable materials engineered to endure high everyday energy.',
    designChallenge: 'The spatial challenge lay in creating a harmonious transition between two completely distinct design languages under one roof: the understated, monolithic serenity of the adult living spaces and the whimsical, energetic architecture of the children\'s quarters. Functionally, storage was a critical issue; family life generates significant sports gear, toys, and tech accessories that threatened to overwhelm the home\'s clean sightlines. The team had to engineer extensive concealed architectural storage throughout corridors and living areas, while selecting performance upholstery fabrics that repel spills without sacrificing tactile luxury.',
    approach: 'Paula & Amanda Ambrósio unified the home through a continuous foundation of white oak chevron flooring and soft warm white plaster walls, establishing a timeless backdrop that flows from room to room. In the main salon, low-profile Italian seating in high-performance Crypton bouclé pairs with a custom oak credenza and a monolithic Calacatta quartz coffee table that withstands everyday family use.\n\nThe kitchen was configured as the active family nerve center, featuring a massive waterfall quartz island with an integrated breakfast counter where children do homework while parents prepare meals. Concealed pantry storage and appliance garages keep countertops pristine.\n\nIn the children\'s wing, the studio designed custom architectural bunk beds fabricated from solid maple, featuring integrated reading niches, acoustic soundproofing, hidden pull-out trundles, and concealed ladder drawers. Custom wallpaper murals and whimsical light fixtures impart individual personality to each child\'s room while maintaining refined craftsmanship.\n\nThe adult primary suite was designed as a tranquil escape on the private end of the floorplan, featuring fluted oak wall paneling, acoustic drapery, and a spa bathroom with a freestanding tub overlooking the yacht marina.',
    materialsNarrative: 'Material selections for HOME IT emphasize family-resilient performance without compromising sensory refinement. Engineered European white oak in a classic chevron pattern offers high dimensional stability against coastal humidity. Living room seating is upholstered in contract-grade Crypton and performance linen fabrics that resist stains and moisture while feeling as soft as cashmere. Countertops utilize non-porous honed Calacatta Gold quartz that resists etching from citrus and spills. Children\'s millwork features water-based non-toxic lacquer finishes and solid hardwood construction.',
