    clientVision: 'A boutique hospitality group commissioned the complete transformation of a landmark Art Deco building on Ocean Drive into an ultra-exclusive 24-suite sanctuary and private members\' wellness lounge. Their ambition was to offer a sophisticated alternative to South Beach\'s raucous nightlife culture, introducing an oasis of understated Mediterranean indulgence, acoustic quietude, and restorative wellness. Guests needed to experience a seamless sensory narrative: transitioning from the vibrant Atlantic beachfront into a serene, dimly lit arrival lounge scented with amber and cedar, before retiring to residential-caliber suites appointed with custom artisan furnishings and spa-inspired baths.',
    designChallenge: 'Transforming a historic 1930s commercial structure into a luxury boutique hotel involves stringent commercial building codes, ADA accessibility, and strict life-safety egress requirements—all while preserving the intimate tactility of a private residential club. Acoustically, the property sits along a bustling corridor; insulating guest rooms from external street noise required engineering multi-pane acoustic glazing and decoupled interior partition walls. Furthermore, commercial hospitality FF&E requires high-traffic commercial durability ratings (CAL 133 fire codes and 100,000+ double rub Martindale ratings) without appearing stiff, corporate, or artificial.',
    approach: 'Paula & Amanda Ambrósio approached the property through the lens of atmospheric choreography. We established a sensory threshold at the arrival foyer, where custom-poured Venetian terrazzo in warm cream aggregate and brass divider strips guides guests into the mood-lit cocktail lounge. The bar is anchored by a sculptural fluted walnut counter with a leathered Verde Saint Denis marble top and back-lit bronze bottle niches.\n\nAcoustics were addressed by deploying textured acoustic plaster ceilings and upholstered wall panels in contract-grade Crypton velvet throughout public spaces, absorbing ambient clatter while enabling intimate vocal conversation. The lighting scheme operates on programmed astronomical clocks, dimming to an intimate 2200K candle-glow as dusk settles over South Beach.\n\nIn the guest suites, we eschewed generic hotel furnishings in favor of bespoke residential designs. Each room features a custom solid teak canopy bed dressed in Italian organic linen, floating stone nightstands with integrated charging niches, and custom woven wicker armchairs. Bathrooms were conceived as wet-room sanctuaries with monolithic cast concrete sinks, floor-to-ceiling microcement, and rain showers equipped with organic botanical amenities.',
    materialsNarrative: 'The material choices for The Aurelia prioritize commercial longevity while preserving intimate residential warmth. Poured Venetian terrazzo incorporates aggregate from Italian Carrara and Verona marble, ground and polished on site with solid brass divider joints. Architectural millwork was crafted from solid FSC-certified Teak and American Walnut, treated with matte commercial-grade urethane sealers that resist spills. Upholstery textiles utilize contract-grade heavy bouclés, Crypton-treated velvets, and top-grain woven saddle leathers that age beautifully with heavy guest turnover.',
